We opened the ceiling along the east conference corridor on Thursday and fo=
und it in about twenty minutes. The condensate drain serving fan coil unit =
FC-2-14 has a failed slip joint at the elbow above grid F-7, and the second=
ary drain pan is corroded through at the outlet. Water has been running dow=
n the back of the partition and tracking under the flooring on the topping =
slab.<br />
<br />
The pattern matches perfectly. The affected band is exactly the run of the =
leak, and the flooring outside that band is sound. This is a maintenance fa=
ilure in the mechanical system and has nothing to do with the substrate or =
with the flooring assembly.<br />
<br />
I would have the unit's drain line rebuilt and the pan replaced before anyo=
ne replaces a square foot of plank, or you will be doing this twice.